- Scope invariance of the prose as well as of the artefacts: this region
  references no successor namespace, no newer framework generation, no typed
  JavaScript dialect and no module bundler.  None of them is part of this
  migration.  The framework generation is unchanged by design, so a captured
  banner naming a newer one would be a finding rather than a detail.  The
  outgoing package manager is named nowhere in this region and nothing here
  presents it as a prerequisite or a recommendation.
- Mirror obligation.  The counterpart is baseline/startup/jpa-init.log: the same
  filename, the same field set in the same order, and the same region-selection
  rule stated above, so that a recursive diff between the two capture
  directories is mechanically meaningful.  Only two field values differ
  legitimately - the runtime label, which reads Java 17 here against JDK 8
  there, and the commit descriptor.  No field was added on this side that the
  counterpart lacks.  A field added on one side only, a region selected
  differently on one side only, or a persistence logging level configured
  differently on one side only would each register as a difference that carries
  no behavioural signal at all.
